### Spring Security & Protected Endpoints Tests
### This file tests JWT authentication and authorization

### Variables (Update these after signup/login)
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080/api
@token = eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.YOUR_JWT_TOKEN_HERE

###############################################
### PUBLIC ENDPOINTS (No Authentication)
###############################################

### 1. Health Check (Public)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health
Accept: application/json

###

### 2. Signup (Public)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "securitytest",
  "email": "security@example.com",
  "password": "test123456",
  "fullName": "Security Test User"
}

###

### 3. Login (Public)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "usernameOrEmail": "securitytest",
  "password": "test123456"
}

###

###############################################
### PROTECTED ENDPOINTS - Without Token (Should Fail with 401)
###############################################

### 4. Get Current User - No Token (Should return 401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Accept: application/json

###

### 5. Get Repositories - No Token (Should return 401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/repositories
Accept: application/json

###

### 6. Get Pull Requests - No Token (Should return 401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/pull-requests
Accept: application/json

###

### 7. Trigger Analysis - No Token (Should return 401)
POST {{baseUrl}}/analysis/trigger
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "prId": "12345"
}

###

###############################################
### PROTECTED ENDPOINTS - With Invalid Token (Should Fail with 401)
###############################################

### 8. Get Current User - Invalid Token (Should return 401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer invalid.jwt.token

###

### 9. Get Repositories - Invalid Token (Should return 401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/repositories
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer invalid.token.here

###

###############################################
### PROTECTED ENDPOINTS - With Valid Token (Should Succeed with 200)
###############################################

### 10. Get Current User - With Valid Token
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 11. Get All Repositories - With Valid Token
GET {{baseUrl}}/repositories
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 12. Get Repository by ID - With Valid Token
GET {{baseUrl}}/repositories/repo123
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 13. Add Repository - With Valid Token
POST {{baseUrl}}/repositories
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "name": "test-repo",
  "url": "https://github.com/user/repo"
}

###

### 14. Get All Pull Requests - With Valid Token
GET {{baseUrl}}/pull-requests
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 15. Get Pull Request by ID - With Valid Token
GET {{baseUrl}}/pull-requests/pr123
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 16. Get Pull Requests by Repository - With Valid Token
GET {{baseUrl}}/pull-requests/repository/repo123
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 17. Trigger AI Analysis - With Valid Token
POST {{baseUrl}}/analysis/trigger
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "prId": "pr123",
  "repository": "test-repo"
}

###

### 18. Get Analysis Results - With Valid Token
GET {{baseUrl}}/analysis/results/pr123
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

### 19. Get Analysis Status - With Valid Token
GET {{baseUrl}}/analysis/status/analysis123
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###

###############################################
### EDGE CASES
###############################################

### 20. Malformed Authorization Header (Should return 401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Accept: application/json
Authorization: InvalidFormat

###

### 21. Bearer Token with Extra Spaces (Should handle gracefully)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer  {{token}}

###

### 22. Empty Authorization Header (Should return 401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Accept: application/json
Authorization: 

###

### 23. Expired Token Test (Should return 401)
# Note: Use a token that's older than 24 hours
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Accept: application/json
Authorization: Bearer EXPIRED_TOKEN_HERE

###

###############################################
### CORS Tests (From Different Origins)
###############################################

### 24. OPTIONS Request (CORS Preflight)
OPTIONS {{baseUrl}}/repositories
Origin: http://localhost:3000
Access-Control-Request-Method: GET
Access-Control-Request-Headers: Authorization

###

###############################################
### TESTING INSTRUCTIONS
###############################################

# STEP 1: Start the application
# .\mvnw.cmd spring-boot:run

# STEP 2: Test public endpoints (1-3)
# Should work without authentication

# STEP 3: Get JWT token from login response (Test #3)
# Copy the accessToken value

# STEP 4: Update @token variable at top with your JWT token

# STEP 5: Test protected endpoints without token (4-7)
# All should return 401 Unauthorized

# STEP 6: Test protected endpoints with invalid token (8-9)
# All should return 401 Unauthorized

# STEP 7: Test protected endpoints with valid token (10-19)
# All should return 200 OK with data

# STEP 8: Test edge cases (20-23)
# Should handle gracefully with proper error messages

###
